  "description": "An MCP (modelcontextprotocol.io) server that serves a local, offline snapshot of the Mantine v7 documentation over stdio. Built on the official @modelcontextprotocol/sdk; reads its data from bundled local files instead of fetching from mantine.dev.",
  "dist-tags": {
   "latest": "1.2.8"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/luis-neira/mtn7-mcp-server",
  "keywords": [
   "mcp",
   "modelcontextprotocol",
   "mantine",
   "documentation"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "maintainers": [
   {
    "email": "[redacted-email:a95eef405e5e]",
    "name": "luis-neira"
   }
  ],
  "name": "@luis-neira/mtn7-mcp-server",
  "readme": "# mtn7-mcp-server\n\nAn [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server that serves a **local, offline\nsnapshot** of the [Mantine](https://mantine.dev) v7.17.8 documentation over stdio.\n\nIt is a fork of `@mantine/mcp-server`, rebuilt on the official\n[`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk).\nUnlike the original, it does **not** fetch from `mantine.dev` at runtime \u2014 all\ndocumentation is bundled in the package and read from local files, so the server\nworks completely offline.\n\nThe bundled snapshot describes a fixed Mantine version (currently **7.17.8**) and\ncovers **331 items** across four kinds \u2014 components, hooks, guides/concept pages\n(theming, styles, etc.), and package overviews. Guidance returned by the server\nreflects that version only; to refresh it, regenerate `public/mcp` and republish.\nCall `get_version` to confirm the exact version and item count at runtime.\n\n## Usage\n\nRun directly with `npx` (requires Node.js **\u2265 22**):\n\n```sh\nnpx @luis-neira/mtn7-mcp-server@latest\n```\n\nThe server speaks the MCP protocol over **stdio** \u2014 it is meant to be launched by\nan MCP client, not used interactively.\n\n### MCP client configuration\n\nAdd it to your client's MCP server config (e.g. Claude Desktop's\n`claude_desktop_config.json`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"mantine-v7-mcp\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@luis-neira/mtn7-mcp-server@latest\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Tools\n\n| Tool             | Description                                                                                      |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `list_items`     | List documentation items. Filter by `kind`, `package`, free-text `query`, and `limit`. Defaults to `kind: component`. |\n| `search_docs`    | Free-text search across the docs, returning ranked matches. Searches **all kinds** unless `kind` is given. |\n| `get_item_doc`   | Get the LLM-ready markdown documentation for an item by name or id.                              |\n| `get_item_props` | Get normalized props metadata for an item by name or id (guides and packages have no props).     |\n| `get_version`    | Report the bundled Mantine version, item count, and snapshot metadata.                            |\n\n`kind` accepts `component`, `hook`, `guide`, or `package`. On `get_item_doc` /\n`get_item_props`, `kind` is only a tiebreaker \u2014 a lookup resolves across the whole\nindex, so an item is still found if it lives under a different kind than expected.\n\nWhen a direct lookup misses, the server does not return a bare \"not found\".\nInstead it runs a cross-kind search and returns the closest matches plus a\nno-network directive, so the client stays inside this offline snapshot rather than\nfalling back to the public web.\n\n## Development\n\n```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run build         # compiles src/ -> dist/ (ESM, NodeNext)\nnpm test              # runs the borp test suite (src/test/**/*.test.ts)\nnpm run format:check  # biome check\nnpm run format:fix    # biome check --write\nnpm run ci            # build + format:check + test\nnpm run verify:data   # sanity-check the bundled public/mcp data\n```\n\nThe package is **ESM** (`\"type\": \"module\"`, TypeScript `module: NodeNext`).\n\nThe data lives in `public/mcp/`: a primary `index.json` (components) plus\nsupplemental `hooks-index.json`, `guides-index.json`, and `packages-index.json`\n(the data client merges every `*-index.json` file), a `version.json`, and one\n`components/<id>.json` per item holding its markdown and props. Paths are resolved\nrelative to the built output, so the data ships in the npm tarball and is found\nregardless of the working directory `npx` launches from. The `generate:*` scripts\nin `scripts/` rebuild these files from source.\n\n`dist/` is a build artifact (git-ignored). `prepublishOnly` runs `npm run ci`\n(build + format:check + test) before publishing. When smoke-testing a tarball with\n`npm pack`, run `npm run build` first, since `prepublishOnly` only fires on\n`npm publish`.\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
